Apple playback bridge ideas follow the iRingo Apple TV ecosystem:
  https://github.com/NSRingo/TV
This project does not distribute the complete iRingo regional/storefront logic.

Runtime dependency copyrights and full license notices for bundled npm packages
are generated into plugin/scripts/LICENSES.txt on every build. Dependencies
include NanoCat utilities/URL helpers and crypto-js; their copyrights remain with
their respective owners.

To make builds possible without a GitHub Packages credential, the actual utility
and URL source packages used in the working integration are vendored in vendor/:
  @nsnanocat/util — package metadata version 1.8.9 — Apache-2.0
    https://github.com/NSNanoCat/util
  @nsnanocat/url — package metadata version 1.2.4 — Apache-2.0
    https://github.com/NSNanoCat/url
Their source, original package metadata and license notices are included.

Project modifications include Apple-focused Loon rules, manual subtitle tracks,
Gemini cue-preserving translation, local caching/concurrency coordination,
live-caption exclusion, Apple playback metadata bridging, and an optional
self-hosted SubDL/Gemini subtitle gateway with CC-based timing calibration.
The source files under src/ represent a modified downstream version of Universal.

